    "question": "In triangle $ABC$, $|BC| = 10$ cm and the perpendicular distance from $A$ to $BC$ is $6$ cm.\n$|AC| = 8$ cm.\nFind the perpendicular distance from $B$ to $AC$.",
    "level": "ordinary",
    "marks": 5,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Find the area using base $[BC]$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Area is half the base times the perpendicular height."
        },
        {
         "tex": "|\\triangle ABC| &= \\tfrac{1}{2}(10)(6)",
         "sym": "Rational(1,2)*10*6"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 30 \\text{ cm}^2",
         "sym": "30"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Use base $[AC]$ (Theorem 16)",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "By Theorem 16, base × height is the same for every side, so the area is the same using $[AC]$ as base. Let $h$ be the height from $B$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "\\tfrac{1}{2}(8)h &= 30",
         "sym": "Eq(4*h, 30)",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "4h &= 30",
         "sym": "Eq(4*h, 30)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Solve for $h$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "h &= \\tfrac{30}{4}",
         "sym": "Eq(h, Rational(30,4))"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 7.5 \\text{ cm}",
         "sym": "Eq(h, Rational(15,2))"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "7.5 \\text{ cm}"
    },
    "finalSym": "Rational(15,2)",
    "answerSym": "2*Rational(1,2)*10*6/8"
   },
